# apps/merchant_app/.easignore
# EAS archives from the monorepo GIT ROOT, so every path here is git-root-relative.
# Goal: upload ONLY what the merchant build needs (apps/merchant_app + shared packages/),
# not the whole monorepo. Without this file EAS fell back to .gitignore and uploaded ~283 MB
# (all apps + backend + dashboards + partnersite + cxsite), which failed on upload.
#
# Root-level dirs are ANCHORED with a leading "/" so a bare name never strips an identically
# named subdir INSIDE apps/merchant_app (e.g. its own services/, scripts/) — the exact trap
# documented in the root .easignore.

# --- Other apps / web projects (not needed for the merchant build) ---
/apps/customer_app/
/apps/gatimitra-riderApp/
/rider-web/

# --- Backend / dashboards / web / infra (never needed for a mobile build) ---
/backend/
/dashboard/
/dashboards/
/partnersite/
/cxsite/
/services/
/infra/
/docs/
/scripts/
/merchant_db/

# --- node_modules anywhere (EAS installs deps on the builder) ---
**/node_modules/

# --- Native dirs: managed workflow; EAS runs expo prebuild ---
/apps/merchant_app/android/
/apps/merchant_app/ios/

# --- Caches / build artifacts ---
**/.expo/
**/.expo-shared/
**/.gradle/
**/.next/
**/.cache/
**/build/
**/out/
**/tmp/
**/temp/
**/logs/
*.log
*.tgz
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa
*.keystore

# --- Backend-only artifacts, docs, tests ---
**/drizzle/
**/__tests__/
**/*.test.*
**/*.spec.*
**/coverage/

# --- Env files: provided via EAS environment, not the archive ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --- Git / IDE / OS junk ---
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- dist/: exclude everything EXCEPT shared workspace package builds ---
# merchant imports @gatimitra/{bill-print,contracts,expo-push-kit,kot-print,
# map-tracking-engine,merchant-payout,otp-verify-ui,print-utils} → they resolve to
# packages/<pkg>/dist, so those MUST stay in the archive.
**/dist/
!packages/*/dist/
!packages/*/dist/**

# NOTE: google-services.json is intentionally NOT ignored here — the merchant Android
# build needs it for FCM (app.config.js wires it via android.googleServicesFile).
